<title>FRANCE: Elf in talks with unions over strike.</title>
<headline>Elf in talks with unions over strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talks continued at Elf Aquitaine's Paris headquarters on Thursday over a week-old strike crippling the company's French refineries, union and company sources said.</p>
<p>Talks over pay and working conditions began at 1400 GMT and were still in progress just over three hours later, they said.</p>
<p>The meeting started amid union demands for employment to be the main focus, but with Elf apparently refusing to discuss a plan to lay off 330 refining staff, which sparked the strike.</p>
<p>One union official said a breakthrough was not excluded.</p>
<p>&quot;I hope this meeting will lead to some way out,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The strike is halting output at Elf's three French plants.</p>
</text>
